{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicityLieRank","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicityLieRank","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.Rank","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.Classical","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.CartanExists","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.Abelian","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_subalgebra_rank_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_subalgebra_rank_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":435,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L435-L486","doc":"**Tier-B assembly: every subalgebra `𝔤 ⊆ 𝔰𝔩₂` has `rank 𝔤 ≤ 1`.** Over an infinite field a\nCartan subalgebra `H = engel_𝔤 x` exists (nilpotent), and `rank 𝔤 ≤ finrank H`\n(`rank_le_finrank_engel`). If `H` is nontrivial its center is nonzero\n(`non_trivial_center_of_isNilpotent`); a nonzero central `Z` commutes with all of `H`, so under the\ninclusion `ι : H ↪ 𝔰𝔩₂` the whole image lies in `ker(ad (ι Z))`, whose finrank is `≤ 1`\n(`sl2_centralizer_finrank_le_one`). Hence `finrank H ≤ 1`, so `rank 𝔤 ≤ 1`. This is the atomicity\nupper bound `rank G ≤ 1` at the Lie level (`rank G = rank Lie(G)`), for a self-dual rank-2 `V`.\n(The generous heartbeat limits absorb typeclass search over the nested `engel ⊆ 𝔤 ⊆ 𝔰𝔩₂` types.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_abelian_finrank_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_abelian_finrank_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L419-L431","doc":"**Abelian subalgebras of 𝔰𝔩₂ are `≤ 1`-dimensional.** Any nonzero element of an abelian\nsubalgebra commutes with the whole subalgebra, so `sl2_finrank_le_one_of_central` applies. (The\nmaximal abelian — Cartan/toral — subalgebras of 𝔰𝔩₂ are exactly the `1`-dimensional ones.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_finrank_le_one_of_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_finrank_le_one_of_central","kind":"theorem","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L400-L417","doc":"**Central-element reduction (the Tier-B bridge).** A subalgebra `A ⊆ 𝔰𝔩₂` containing a\nnonzero element `X` that commutes with all of `A` has `finrank A ≤ 1` — because `A ⊆ ker (ad X)`,\nwhose finrank is `≤ 1` (`sl2_centralizer_finrank_le_one`). Both the abelian case (any nonzero\n`X ∈ A`) and the nilpotent case (a nonzero central element, via\n`non_trivial_center_of_isNilpotent`) feed this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_centralizer_finrank_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_centralizer_finrank_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L389-L398","doc":"**Corollary: the centralizer of a nonzero `X ∈ 𝔰𝔩₂` has `finrank ≤ 1`.** Immediate from\n`sl2_ker_ad_le_span` (`ker (ad X) ≤ K ∙ X`) and `finrank (K ∙ X) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_ker_ad_le_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_ker_ad_le_span","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L295-L387","doc":"**Tier-B keystone: the centralizer of a nonzero `X ∈ 𝔰𝔩₂` is at most 1-dimensional.**\n`ker (ad X) ≤ K ∙ X` — a matrix commuting with a nonzero traceless `2×2` matrix is a scalar\nmultiple of it. In coordinates `⁅X, y⁆ = 0` is the vanishing of the cross product\n`(X₀₀,X₀₁,X₁₀) × (y₀₀,y₀₁,y₁₀)`, forcing collinearity. Needs `2 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_rank_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_rank_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L267-L293","doc":"**The rank of `𝔰𝔩₂` is exactly `1`.** Combines the upper bound `sl2_rank_le_one`\nwith the lower bound `1 ≤ rank`: over an infinite field a regular element `x` exists,\n`rank = finrank (engel x)`, and that regular `x` is nonzero (were `x = 0`, `engel 0 = ⊤`\nwould force `rank = finrank 𝔰𝔩₂ = 3 > 1`), so `x ∈ engel x` makes `engel x` nontrivial,\ngiving `finrank ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_finrank_engel_h_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_finrank_engel_h_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L257-L265","doc":"**Cartan dimension of `𝔰𝔩₂` is `1`.** The Engel subalgebra (generalized `0`-eigenspace\nof `ad h`) at the regular diagonal `h` has `finrank = 1`, since\n`finrank (engel h) = natTrailingDegree (charpoly (ad h)) = 1`\n(`LieAlgebra.finrank_engel`). This is the reusable toral-dimension datum for `𝔰𝔩₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_ntd_ad_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_ntd_ad_h","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L226-L255","doc":"The trailing degree of `charpoly (ad h)` is exactly `1`: the constant coefficient\nof `X³ − 4X` vanishes (0 is a root — `h` centralizes itself) while the degree-1\ncoefficient `−4 ≠ 0`. Needs `2 ≠ 0` so that `4 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_charpoly_ad_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_charpoly_ad_h","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L212-L224","doc":"The characteristic polynomial of `ad h` on `𝔰𝔩₂` is `X³ − 4X`\n(eigenvalues `0, 2, −2` on the basis `(h, e, f)`). Factored out of `sl2_rank_le_one`\nso the trailing-degree and Cartan-dimension results share it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_rank_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_rank_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L181-L210","doc":"**T3-lie CLOSED — `rank 𝔰𝔩₂ ≤ 1`** (over a field with `2 ≠ 0`, e.g. the\ncharacteristic-zero substrate). Chain: the frame\n(`rank ≤ natTrailingDegree (charpoly (ad h))`), basis-independence of `charpoly`\n(`charpoly_toMatrix`), the diagonal `toMatrix` (`sl2_toMatrix_ad_h`), and\n`charpoly (diagonal ![0,2,−2]) = ∏(X − C dᵢ) = X³ − 4X` whose trailing\ncoefficient (degree 1) is `−4 ≠ 0`. This is the atomicity **upper bound** on the\nLie side — the piece the elementary group route could not reach. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_toMatrix_ad_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_toMatrix_ad_h","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L157-L179","doc":"**`ad h` is `diag(0,2,−2)` in the `(h,e,f)` basis.** Each basis vector is an\neigenvector (`sl2_ad_h_*`), so the matrix is diagonal with the eigenvalues. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_ad_h_f","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_ad_h_f","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L153-L155","doc":"`ad h (f) = −2f` — eigenvalue `−2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_ad_h_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_ad_h_e","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L149-L151","doc":"`ad h (e) = 2e` — eigenvalue `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_ad_h_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_ad_h_h","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L145-L147","doc":"`ad h (h) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2Basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2Basis","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L131-L141","doc":"**The 𝔰𝔩₂ basis `(h,e,f)`** — from linear independence (`sl2_linindep`) and\nspanning (`sl2_decomp`). Gives `finrank R 𝔰𝔩₂ = 3`, `Module.Free`, and unblocks\n`charpoly (ad h)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_linindep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_linindep","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L114-L129","doc":"**Linear independence** of the 𝔰𝔩₂ triple `(h,e,f)` — read `g₀=g₁=g₂=0` off the\n`(0,0)/(0,1)/(1,0)` entries of a vanishing combination. With `sl2_decomp`\n(spanning) this makes `(h,e,f)` a basis of `𝔰𝔩₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L99-L112","doc":"**Trace-zero coordinates.** Every `x ∈ 𝔰𝔩₂` decomposes on the triple as\n`x = x₀₀·h + x₀₁·e + x₁₀·f` — the `(1,1)` entry is `−x₀₀` by tracelessness. This\nis the constructive spanning statement for the basis `(h,e,f)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_bracket_h_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_bracket_h_h","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L93-L97","doc":"**`[h,h] = 0`** — the Cartan element is `ad`-fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_bracket_h_f","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_bracket_h_f","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L83-L91","doc":"**`[h,f] = −2f`** — the lowering eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_bracket_h_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_bracket_h_e","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L73-L81","doc":"**`[h,e] = 2e`** — the raising eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2H","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L70-L71","doc":"`h = diag(1,−1) ∈ 𝔰𝔩₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2F","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L68-L69","doc":"`f = E₁₀ ∈ 𝔰𝔩₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2E","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2E","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L66-L67","doc":"`e = E₀₁ ∈ 𝔰𝔩₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.rank_le_one_of_ad_charpoly_trailing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.rank_le_one_of_ad_charpoly_trailing","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityLieRank.lean#L35-L51","doc":"**Lie-rank route to the atomicity upper bound (frame).** If a Lie algebra `L`\nover `R` carries an element `x` whose `ad`-characteristic polynomial has\ntrailing degree `≤ 1`, then `rank R L ≤ 1`. Immediate from Mathlib's\nspecific-element rank bound `rank_le_natTrailingDegree_charpoly_ad`.\n\nThis is the closeable reframing of the atomicity residual: with `rank G =\nrank Lie(G)` it replaces the (Mathlib-absent) algebraic-group root count by a\nLie-algebra charpoly computation. Applied to `𝔰𝔩₂` and the regular diagonal\n`h` (whose `ad h` charpoly is `X³ − 4X`, trailing degree 1) it yields\n`rank 𝔰𝔩₂ ≤ 1` — the atomicity upper bound. The concrete `𝔰𝔩₂` computation is\nthe remaining core (bean `qou-atsd-t3-lie`); no instance is fabricated here. ","signatureChunk":0}]}